 # Asymmetric Lobe Approximation
 
-Also called: Asymmetric Lobe, 1D Lobe Approximation
 
 ## Overview
-Asymmetric Lobe Approximation is a method for accelerating multiple scattering calculations in participating media by replacing full 4D spherical phase function lobes with asymmetric 1D functions [S1]. It solves the high computational cost of evaluating full angular scattering distributions by focusing on the dominant multiple scattering component, which is less sensitive to angular precision than double scattering [S1]. It differs from sibling methods like [Beam Spreading Width Model](1193-beam-spreading-width-model.md) and [PSF-based Multiple Scattering Rendering](1297-psf-based-multiple-scattering-rendering.md) by explicitly simplifying the angular representation of the scattering lobe itself rather than just the spatial spread or point spread function [S1].
